---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';

const principles = [
  {
    title: 'Blast radius before feature velocity',
    text: 'Every change to production infrastructure, whether an Exchange migration, a BIOS update or an MFA rollout, goes through ring-based deployment: canary, pilot, broad, all. Not because it is slower, but because the cost of a failed change across a whole fleet is orders of magnitude higher than the wait for controlled validation. Attestree turns that procedure into a product.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Evidence before trust',
    text: 'An artifact that was installed “because the CDN said so” leaves the auditor’s question unanswered months later. So software is checked before rollout, not scanned after installation: run in a sandbox, recorded as an observed SBOM and backed by a signed statement. A decision that cannot be evidenced is an assumption.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Automate the known, architect the complex',
    text: 'Automation is not a goal in itself. What I understand well and what repeats belongs in a pipeline: configuration deployment, compliance checks, onboarding workflows. What I do not yet fully understand deserves an architecture decision first, not premature automation that does the wrong thing faster.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Hybrid is a strategy, not a compromise',
    text: 'Hybrid architecture does not come from an inability to migrate fully to the cloud. It is a deliberate choice when on-premises infrastructure meets regulatory, performance or cost requirements that a pure cloud solution cannot. The bridge architecture of the Exchange migration and the hybrid identity solution were coexistence strategies, not stepping stones.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Observability before optimisation',
    text: 'You cannot optimise what you cannot see. Before I fix performance problems or change processes, I build the visibility: central log aggregation, compliance dashboards, real-time alerting. The SIEM build was not a security project that happened to produce monitoring. It was the foundation every later operational decision could rest on.',
  },
  {
    title: 'The destructive step stays with a person',
    text: 'Automation proposes, people approve. A rollback, a quarantine, a release under a new signing certificate: the system stops and presents the evidence instead of guessing. Where a mistake hits the whole fleet, confirmation is not friction. It is the point where responsibility becomes visible.',
  },
];
---

<PageLayout title="Architectural Principles — Marc Borer" description="Six principles that guide Marc Borer’s architecture decisions: from ring-based rollout and evidence before trust to a deliberate hybrid strategy." ogImage="/og/principles.png">
  <header class="page-head">
    <span class="eyebrow">Principles</span>
    <h1>Six convictions, learned in operations.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Shaped by building and running business-critical infrastructure and, since 2026, by building a platform that enforces exactly these principles for other fleets.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <ol class="principles" role="list">
      {principles.map((p, i) => (
        <li class="principle">
          <span class="principle-index" aria-hidden="true">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
          <div class="principle-body">
            <h2 class="principle-title">{p.title}</h2>
            <p class="principle-text">{p.text}</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </section>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .principles {
    display: grid;
    max-width: 60rem;
  }

  .principle {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 6rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-6);
    padding-block: var(--space-8);
    border-bottom: var(--rule) solid var(--hairline);
  }

  .principle-index {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-stretch: 125%;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    padding-top: 0.1em;
  }

  .principle-body {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  .principle-title {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
  }

  .principle-text {
    line-height: var(--leading-prose);
    color: var(--ink-2);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .principle {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-3);
    }

    .principle-index {
      font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    }
  }
</style>
